<title>USA: Ag attache - Malaysia growing market for U.S. soy.</title>
<headline>Ag attache - Malaysia growing market for U.S. soy.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>An expanding livestock sector has turned Malaysia into an important market for soybeans and soymeal and the U.S. is poised to capture a large share, an U.S. agricultural attache said.</p>
<p>In a report dated February 26 released in Washington Wednesday, the attache predicted U.S. soybeans would capture 85% of the Malaysia import market in 1996/97 and 80% in 1997/98.</p>
<p>The attache also estimated soymeal imports from the U.S. would climb to 50,000 tonnes and 70,000 tonnes in 1996/97 and 1997/98 respectively, up from 35,000 tonnes in 1995/96, when Malaysia started importing U.S. soymeal.</p>
<p>Attache reports are not official USDA data.</p>
</text>
